_b3("""quote:'"Tell me, Muse, of the man of twists and turns." The cunning king of Ithaca devised the Trojan Horse, then spent ten years and a hundred hardships fighting his way home to Penelope.'""","""quote:'"The way home is the only teacher; every shore is a mirror." Odysseus gave his name to no one and wore a hundred masks, for he knew that a self unbroken by the sea is merely a self unborn.'""")
_b3("""quote:'"Nine nights I hung from the windswept tree, wounded by my own spear, given to Odin, myself to myself." The Allfather gave an eye and hung from Yggdrasil to learn the runes.'""","""quote:'"Wisdom is bought in the coin of the self." Odin gave an eye to the well and nine nights to the tree, and learned that whatever is held back from the sacrifice is never truly owned.'""")
